  "provenance": {
    "method": "One minus the cosine similarity between a residue's mean-removed ESM-2 embedding and the nearer of two mean-removed centroids, one for helix and one for sheet. Centroids are means over residues in runs of helical or extended backbone torsions, taken from AlphaFold DB models and restricted to residues with pLDDT at or above 80. A heuristic, not a trained model.",
    "why_not_euclidean": "Euclidean distance to the nearer centroid separates nothing here (Cohen's d -0.023). The two centroids are 1.32 apart against a within-class spread of 4.60, so relative to the noise they are the same point, and the measurement is dominated by a global mean every residue shares. Removing that mean and comparing directions gives Cohen's d +1.024.",
